  "reason": null,
  "outcome": null,
  "reads_an_outcome": false,
  "needs_before_research_data": "RunInputs.inventory_inputs_are (research data is refused by the module's guard unless the gate file exists and the run is authorized). side.q needs nonres_mwh including 2009 to 2011; side.dose needs dc_gwh (base_retail_gwh is no longer read). The history of the inventory is settled by Joe's ruling of 2026-11-20 (D-119), in his words: \"Use the inventory as built, the load history underlying the headline design, for the inventory-against-sales check.\" The check is given the inventory as built, which this registry supplies as RunInputs.side.dose, the dose frame the headline design's sets are split on (inventory_against_sales.INVENTORY_HISTORY_D119). The check cannot detect a frame built from another history, since it takes whatever frame it is given, so the registry establishes it before the check is called, in two ways (session 27): equal content by hash, run_outcomes.frame_fingerprint(side.dose) against RunInputs.inventory_as_built.dose_fingerprint, the stamp taken when the sets were split; and the headline set split again from the frame, design.split on side.q and side.dose giving exactly the hosts with their cohorts and the comparison-eligible units of RunInputs.sets. On research data RunInputs.inventory_as_built is required and a substituted split function is refused; a mismatch is refused in words and the check is not run.",
